{"assets":["/statement-assets/da389ad780be886a7b72a0f2b334436a15044058081f7db7306f01f0181c94b7.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"630","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. A rectangle"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"0.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"64 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Developing tools for creation of locations maps for turn-based fights in a new game, Petya faced the following problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A field map consists of hexagonal cells. Since locations sizes are going to be big, a game designer wants to have a tool for quick filling of a field part with identical enemy units. This action will look like following: a game designer will select a rectangular area on the map, and each cell whose center belongs to the selected rectangle will be filled with the enemy unit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, if a game designer selected cells having coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x2, y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1 ≤ x2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1 ≤ y2"},{"kind":"text","text":", then all cells having center coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1 ≤ x ≤ x2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1 ≤ y ≤ y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be filled. Orthogonal coordinates system is set up so that one of cell sides is parallel to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"OX"},{"kind":"text","text":" axis, all hexagon centers have integer coordinates and for each integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" there are cells having center with such "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinate and for each integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" there are cells having center with such "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" coordinate. It is guaranteed that difference "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2 - x1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Working on the problem Petya decided that before painting selected units he wants to output number of units that will be painted on the map."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help him implement counting of these units before painting."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/da389ad780be886a7b72a0f2b334436a15044058081f7db7306f01f0181c94b7.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of input contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, y1, x2, y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ x1 ≤ x2 ≤ 109,  - 109 ≤ y1 ≤ y2 ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the coordinates of the centers of two cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output one integer — the number of cells to be filled."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1 5 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"13"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"630E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/630/problem/E"}